{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Adjacent field evidence from a cross-source log audit (2026-07-30). Flagging it here because it concerns tracker convergence in CI, but I want to be clear it may be a different mechanism from the one this ticket describes — judge accordingly.\n\nThe `Reconcile Bridge` workflow's \"Commit reconciler events back and push to origin/tickets\" step failed on 4 runs today by exhausting its retry budget:\n\n    Push rejected (attempt 4):\n     ! [rejected]            HEAD -> tickets (fetch first)\n    error: failed to push some refs to 'https://github.com/navapbc/rebar'\n    hint: Updates were rejected because the remote contains work that you do not have\n    Push rejected (attempt 5):\n     ! [rejected]            HEAD -> tickets (fetch first)\n    Push failed after 5 retries. Last stderr: ...\n    ##[error]Process completed with exit code 1.\n\nAffected runs (UTC): 2026-07-30T00:45:55 (30503669644), 03:06:34 (30510284129), 05:02:44 (30515516036), 22:03:07 (30585738860).\n\nWhy it may NOT be this bug: the workflow does attempt to reconverge between retries (`git merge --no-edit origin/tickets`, with an explicit `merge conflict` guard), so this reads as ordinary write contention — `origin/tickets` advancing faster than 5 retries can absorb — rather than a tracker that structurally cannot reconverge under a narrow refspec.\n\nWhy it might still be relevant: it is direct evidence of how often a CI-side clone of the tickets branch fails to catch up to the remote in practice, which is the same convergence surface this ticket reasons about. If the narrow-clone refspec is what the reconcile-bridge job uses, the two could share a cause.\n\nI have filed the workflow-level symptom separately as bug 449f-f9bf-be90-47fe (alert-zebrine-drongo), which covers this push-rejection mode alongside two other Reconcile Bridge failure modes. Linking rather than duplicating: if this turns out to be the same root cause, 449f should be marked a duplicate of this ticket."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785451674402536001,"uuid":"7db4b060-c40b-4581-971f-9aa29607715b"}